g class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/el-escorial.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">El Escorial</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">El Escorial is a vast royal monastery and palace north-west of Madrid, built for Philip II of Spain between 1563 and 1584.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/el-fasher"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/el-fasher.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">El Fasher</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">El Fasher is a city in western Sudan that became the capital of the Darfur Sultanate.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/el-geneina"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/el-geneina.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">El Geneina</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">El Geneina is a city in western Sudan, the capital of West Darfur state, close to the border with Chad.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/el-greco"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/el-greco.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">El Greco</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">El Greco, born Domenikos Theotokopoulos at Candia in Venetian Crete, was a painter who trained in the Cretan school of icon painting before working in Venice and Rome.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/el-hadj-umar-tall"><span class="enc-name">El Hadj Umar Tall</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">El Hadj Umar Tall was a West African Muslim scholar and military leader of the nineteenth century who founded the Toucouleur state through conquests in the 1850s and…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/el-jadida"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/el-jadida.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">El Jadida</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">El Jadida, formerly Mazagan, is a port city on the Atlantic coast of Morocco, south-west of Casablanca.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/el-mirador"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/el-mirador.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">El Mirador</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">El Mirador ('The Lookout') is a large pre-Columbian Maya settlement of the Middle and Late Preclassic period in the north of the department of El Petén, Guatemala.</span></a></li></ul>
